<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Medina</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Medina is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hejaz">Hejaz</a> region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, the second holiest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophet-muhammad">Prophet Muhammad</a> migrated there in 622 and established the first Muslim community. It was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a> until Ali moved his seat to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kufa">Kufa</a>, and later rulers including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> claimed its protection.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/medina.jpg" alt="Medina" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Konevi · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Al-Masjid_An-Nabawi_(Bird%27s_Eye_View).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
